      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra_flavatra_en/",
      "html": "<p>The algae-eating suckermouth barb Garra flavatra from Burma is a quite beautiful fish. In contrast to all other species of algae-eaters this is a species which is kept due to its own attractivity.</p><p>In our show-room the fish now revealed a secret they kept so far: they develope deep red fins!</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra_flavatra_en/",
      "html": "<p>For our customers: we currently have bred ones (416460) and wild collected ones (416461). Please note that we exclusively supply the wholesale market.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra_flavatra_en/",
      "html": "<p>Keeping Garra flavatra is very easy.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra_flavatra_en/",
      "html": "<p>They like water temperatures between 18 and 26°C (better cooler than warmer). The remaining water parameters are of no meaning for them.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra_flavatra_en/",
      "html": "<p>The up to 9 cm long fish are kept best in groups. They are completely peaceful against each other as well as against other species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/garra_flavatra_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Garra: an indigenous name for those fishes in Bengal. flavatra: Latin, means “yellow-black”, referring to the coloration.</p><p>Text &amp; photos: Frank Schäfer</p>"
    }
  ],
